course: dictionary
lesson: 6380
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Mulberry is one of them. The dictionary gives three: a tree, its fruit, and a dark purple-red colour. To find the right meaning, read the words around it. «The silkworm, a caterpillar that eats mulberry leaves, spins silk» means the tree, because leaves grow on trees.
explain: Now try the fruit meaning: «She spread mulberry jam on her toast.» Jam is made from fruit, so mulberry here means the fruit. Ask yourself which meaning fits the clues, then put your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
explain: Sometimes the clue is a colour. «Her scarf was a deep mulberry shade» tells you the word names a colour, not food or a tree. Context clues are always your best guide.
fact: A mulberry is a tree with broad leaves and dark purple, red or white berries.
fact: The mulberry is also the fruit of that tree, and it can name a dark purple-red colour.
fact: Silkworms are the caterpillars of the domestic silk moth, and they eat almost nothing but fresh mulberry leaves.
fact: The Chinese learned to make silk from the cocoons of silkworms, and kept the method secret for centuries.
fact: «Here we go round the mulberry bush» is an old nursery rhyme.
exercise: «Silkworms eat almost nothing but fresh mulberry leaves.» In this sentence, what is a mulberry? | A kind of caterpillar | A dark purple-red colour | *A tree with broad leaves | A type of silk
exercise: «In the lunchbox, Sam ate a bowl of mulberry jam.» What is a mulberry here? | A tree | *The fruit | A nursery rhyme | A colour
exercise: Mia says her new scarf is a mulberry shade. What does mulberry mean here? | A tree with broad leaves | A caterpillar | A berry you can eat | *A dark purple-red colour
test: «The mulberry tree grew by the school gate, its branches full of berries.» Which meaning fits? | A nursery rhyme | Silk thread | A purple-red colour | *A tree
test: What is «Here we go round the mulberry bush» best described as? | A science book | *An old nursery rhyme | A dance | A recipe for jam
exam: In «In a school box, small white caterpillars munch mulberry leaves», what does mulberry mean? | A purple colour | A nursery rhyme | *A tree | A jar of jam
